'''alchemic''' (al-kem′ik), ''a.'' [Formerly ''alchymic'' = F. ''alchimique'', < ML. ''alchimicus'', < ''alchimia'', alchemy: see ''alchemy'', and cf. ''chemic.''] Relating to or produced by alchemy. Formerly also spelled ''alchymic.''
{{smaller block|At last lowered into the semi-conscious ''alchemic'' state wherein misery turns to habit.
{{right|''L. Wallace'', Ben-Hur, p. 138.}}}}

'''alchemical''' (al-kem′i-kal), ''a.'' Same as ''alchemic.''

'''alchemically''' (al-kem′i-ka̤l-i), ''adv.'' In an alchemic manner; by means of alchemy. Formerly also spelled ''alchymically.''
{{smaller block|Lully would prove it ''alchemically.''
{{right|''Camden'', Remains, Money.}}}}

'''alchemist''' (al′ke-mist), ''n.'' [Early mod. E. ''alchymist'', ''alchimist'', ''alcumist'', ''alkemyste'' (also with added term. ''-er''<sup>1</sup>, *''alchemister'', ''alchymister'', ''alchimister'', < ME. ''alcamister'', ''alkamystere'', ''alkamystre''), < OF. ''alkemiste'', ''alquemiste'', mod. F. ''alchimiste'' = Sp. ''alquimista'' = Pg. It. ''alchimista'', < ML. ''alchymista'', < ''alchymia'': see ''alchemy'' and ''-ist.''] One who practises or is versed in alchemy. Formerly also spelled ''alchymist.''
{{smaller block|You are an ''alchymist'', make gold of that.
{{right|''Shak.'', T. of A., v. 1.}}}}

'''alchemister†''', ''n.'' Same as ''alchemist.''

'''alchemistic''' (al-ke-mis′tik), ''a.'' Relating to or practising alchemy.
{{smaller block|Paracelsus informs us that the composition of his “triple panacea” can be described only in the language of ''alchemistic'' adepts. {{right|''Pop. Sci. Mo.'', XX. 64.}}}}

'''alchemistical''' (al-ke-mis′ti-ka̤l), ''a.'' Same as ''alchemistic.''
{{smaller block|Irregular, secular ale, courageous, contagious ale, ''alcumistical'' ale.}}

